{"id":"transamazonica","title":"Transamazônica (BR-230)","who":"Classic route · across the Amazon by motorcycle","when":"June to October (dry season); in the rains it turns to mud","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycle or 4x4, 2–3 weeks","kind":"moto","color":"#9a3412","summary":"The 1970s highway pushed across the Amazon: from the Tocantins at Marabá west past Altamira and the Xingu, Itaituba on the Tapajós, to Humaitá on the Madeira. Long stretches are still dirt, with dust, potholes, mud and wooden bridges; one 2025 couple called it harder than the Andes. A R$1 billion tender (June 2026) is to pave about 125 km between Uruará and Rurópolis.","sources":[{"label":"NSC Total: R$1 billion for asphalt on the Transamazônica (2026)","url":"https://www.nsctotal.com.br/?p=7948870"},{"label":"Portal Amazônia: Amapá couple crosses South America by motorcycle (2025)","url":"https://portalamazonia.com/turismo/andes-casal-ap-cruza-america-sul/"},{"label":"Horizons Unlimited: BR-230, Humaitá and the BR-163","url":"https://horizonsunlimited.com/hubb/south-america/br-230-humaita-br-163-a-72836"}],"approximate":"Main towns; the line follows today's roads, conditions change with every rainy season.","km":2060,"bbox":[-63.0256,-8.0307,-49.1005,-3.0859],"stops":[{"name":"Marabá","place":"Marabá, Pará","at":[-5.3463,-49.1007],"text":"Where the Transamazônica crosses the Tocantins, the start west.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Vista_panor%C3%A2mica_da_Nova_Marab%C3%A1.jpg/500px-Vista_panor%C3%A2mica_da_Nova_Marab%C3%A1.jpg","page":"Marabá, Pará","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_panor%C3%A2mica_da_Nova_Marab%C3%A1.jpg","credit":"Hallel","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Novo Repartimento","place":"Novo Repartimento, Pará","at":[-4.2519,-49.9524],"text":"Past the Tucuruí reservoir."},{"name":"Altamira","place":"Altamira, Pará","at":[-3.2041,-52.21],"text":"The Xingu river and the controversial Belo Monte dam."},{"name":"Rurópolis","place":"Rurópolis, Pará","at":[-4.1014,-54.9087],"text":"Where the BR-230 meets the BR-163."},{"name":"Itaituba","place":"Itaituba, Pará","at":[-4.2625,-55.9878],"text":"On the wide Tapajós; the hardest dirt starts here.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Itaituba.JPG/500px-Itaituba.JPG","page":"Itaituba","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Itaituba.JPG","credit":"Amit Evron","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Jacareacanga","place":"Jacareacanga, Pará","at":[-6.2197,-57.7586],"text":"Deep in the forest on the upper Tapajós.","source":{"label":"Portal Amazônia (2025)","url":"https://portalamazonia.com/turismo/andes-casal-ap-cruza-america-sul/"}},{"name":"Apuí","place":"Apuí, Amazonas","at":[-7.194,-59.883],"text":"Into Amazonas state, cattle frontier and forest.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Amazonas_Municip_Apui.jpg/500px-Amazonas_Municip_Apui.jpg","page":"Apuí","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amazonas_Municip_Apui.jpg","credit":"FrancoBras","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Humaitá","place":"Humaitá, Amazonas","at":[-7.5099,-63.0249],"text":"The Madeira river: tarmac again on the BR-319 or BR-230 west."}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":184,"line":[[-5.3467,-49.1005],[-5.3765,-49.1396],[-5.3708,-49.1899],[-5.2587,-49.3248],[-5.0464,-49.4569],[-4.9733,-49.4433],[-4.9141,-49.4827],[-4.8631,-49.4916],[-4.8599,-49.538],[-4.7992,-49.5714],[-4.7351,-49.6551],[-4.689,-49.6823],[-4.6501,-49.7658],[-4.6064,-49.7683],[-4.5314,-49.8286],[-4.4746,-49.9077],[-4.4224,-49.9362],[-4.252,-49.9523]]},{"by":"ride","km":322,"line":[[-4.252,-49.9523],[-4.2063,-49.9898],[-4.1811,-50.0351],[-4.16,-50.0984],[-4.1574,-50.1937],[-4.1187,-50.2671],[-4.0478,-50.297],[-3.9712,-50.2612],[-3.8612,-50.442],[-3.8297,-50.6829],[-3.7793,-50.8151],[-3.7384,-50.8504],[-3.5138,-51.1648],[-3.422,-51.2507],[-3.2939,-51.4331],[-3.1131,-51.6248],[-3.1047,-51.6473],[-3.1353,-51.7132],[-3